 "findings": {
  "energy_generational": "Model held fixed, M3 Ultra -> M5 Max is 2.15x-3.43x less energy per query (mean ~2.7x) on the ipw benchmark. Monotone M3U > M4Max > M5Max for every model. This is MEASURED consumer-silicon data and can replace the roofline-MODELLED consumer devices in EXP-20260823-01-quarterly-ipj.",
  "accuracy_invariance_CHECK": "toolcall15 accuracy is EXACTLY platform-invariant (0.00 pt spread across M3U/M4Max/M5Max for all 7 models) - the harness is deterministic and this validates it. The ipw benchmark is NOT: up to 15.93 pt spread for identical model+quant on different silicon, which cannot be a hardware effect.",
  "small_N": "ipw accuracy granularity implies tiny evaluation sets (N=27, 15, 18 inferred from the decimal expansions). At N~15-30 a 15.9 pt swing is inside binomial noise. ipw accuracy needs Wilson CIs (roughly +/-15-20 pt) and must NOT be used for cross-platform accuracy claims.",
  "pinchbench_floor": "pinchbench accuracies are 0-21.74% - at or near floor, several exactly 0.0. Energy comparisons remain valid; accuracy comparisons are not discriminative.",
  "DUPLICATE_ROW": "pinchbench has TWO rows for MacBook Pro M5 Max / Qwen3.5 9B (Q4_K_M): 1245.739 J @ 0.0% (power 61.9734) and 1360.6131 J @ 13.04% (power 50.8754). Same platform, model, params and mem. Needs de-duplication at source before use.",
  "M4_MAX_RESOLVED": "A real Mac Studio M4 Max exists in this board. It is NOT the base M4 32GB (Mac16,10) box in the separate base-M4 measurement, which is why the DeepSeek-V4-Flash edge cell was impossible there. Spec section 5 must distinguish the two."
 },
 "caveats": [
  "Energy is J/query on these three benchmarks - NOT TB v2.1 J/task. Do not merge into the TB board without restating the workload.",
  "Quantization is Q4_K_M throughout (AFM-3 excepted); the TB board's local tiers are bf16/FP8. Cross-comparison is quant-confounded.",
  "No harness/engine recorded here (llama.cpp vs MLX). Engine affects J/token materially - see R5."
 ]
}